        "input": "signal = \"ab\", code = \"xyz\"",
        "output": "[]",
        "explanation": "The code length exceeds signal length, so no valid window exists."
      }
    ],
    "solution": {
      "brute_force": {
        "approach": "Slide a window of length len(code) across signal. At each position, sort the window substring and the code and compare. If they match, record the index. Sorting each window takes O(k log k) where k = len(code), giving O(n * k log k) overall.",
        "code": "def find_anagram_positions(signal, code):\n    result = []\n    k = len(code)\n    sorted_code = sorted(code)  # Sort code once\n    for i in range(len(signal) - k + 1):\n        if sorted(signal[i:i+k]) == sorted_code:\n            result.append(i)\n    return result",
        "time": "O(n * k * log k)",
        "space": "O(k)"
      },
      "optimal": {
        "approach": "Use a fixed-size sliding window with two frequency arrays of size 26 (one for code, one for the current window). Initialize both arrays for the first window. As the window slides right by one, increment the count for the incoming character and decrement for the outgoing character. Compare the two frequency arrays in O(26) = O(1) at each step, giving O(n) overall.",
        "code": "def find_anagram_positions(signal, code):\n    result = []\n    k = len(code)\n    n = len(signal)\n    if k > n:\n        return result\n\n    code_freq = [0] * 26\n    window_freq = [0] * 26\n\n    # Build frequency arrays for code and first window\n    for i in range(k):\n        code_freq[ord(code[i]) - ord('a')] += 1\n        window_freq[ord(signal[i]) - ord('a')] += 1\n\n    if window_freq == code_freq:\n        result.append(0)\n\n    # Slide the window one step at a time\n    for i in range(k, n):\n        window_freq[ord(signal[i]) - ord('a')] += 1       # Add incoming char\n        window_freq[ord(signal[i - k]) - ord('a')] -= 1  # Remove outgoing char\n        if window_freq == code_freq:\n            result.append(i - k + 1)\n\n    return result",
